spinescope is research and education software. It is not a medical device and must not be used
for diagnosis or treatment decisions.

Test and example data, where used, come from public datasets under their own licenses, e.g.
SPIDER (van der Graaf et al., Scientific Data 2024, doi:10.1038/s41597-024-03090-w;
dataset doi:10.5281/zenodo.10159290), licensed CC BY 4.0. No such data is redistributed in
this repository unless stated next to it.

Learned spine labeller (optional, `spinescope[ml]`)

The packaged weights `src/spinescope/anatomy/ml/assets/labeller_v1.onnx` and
`src/spinescope/anatomy/lumbosacral_v1.onnx` were trained on the SPIDER lumbar spine MRI dataset
(`lumbosacral_v1.json` holds thresholds from SPIDER training; `calibration_v2.json` was fitted on SPIDER
training and Sudirman; see docs/model_card.md): van der Graaf JW, et al. "Lumbar spine segmentation in MR images: a dataset
and a public benchmark." Scientific Data (2024), doi:10.1038/s41597-024-03090-w; dataset
doi:10.5281/zenodo.10159290. SPIDER is licensed CC BY 4.0. The weights are derived from it and are
distributed with that attribution; no SPIDER images or masks are included in this repository. The
training recipe, data split and held-out results are in docs/model_card.md. Research use only.
